{"uncertainty": 0.15, "outcome": "rtl_bug", "artifacts": [{"kind": "root_cause_analysis", "title": "Root cause: uart_tx reloads its hold register on a start pulse while a frame is in flight", "summary": "Requirement [requirement:req-d10c4df532]. The failure was reproduced upstream: [run:run-0002] reports 1 of 4 checks failed, per [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.triage.e2]. VeriTriage's top hypothesis was 'Likely RTL bug' at only 30% confidence ([run:run-0001], [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.triage.e1]), so it is treated as one candidate, not a conclusion.\n\nDEFECT (read from [artifact:prj-d4a591eb4b.design-under-investigation.a1]): before the state case, the always block has an unconditional `if (start) hold <= data;`. This runs in every state, not only IDLE.\n\nINCORRECTNESS: the file's own header states that a start pulse while a frame is in flight is ignored. The unconditional assignment breaks that contract.\n\nCAUSALITY: the DATA state drives `tx <= hold[bit_idx + 1]`. A start pulse during START or DATA overwrites hold, so every data bit sent after the pulse comes from the new byte. That is a fault in hold, and it becomes visible as a wrong serial byte one or more bit-times later. The checker sees the failure only when it compares the received byte, not at the cycle where hold was written. The IDLE branch already loads hold correctly, so the extra assignment is redundant as well as wrong.\n\nFIX DIRECTION, not applied here: delete the pre-case `if (start) hold <= data;`.\n\nHYPOTHESES, ranked:\n(1) rtl_bug, mid-frame reload of hold. Supported by the code reading and the header contract. Refuted if the attached repro, which pulses start with 8'h3C during data bit 1 of an 8'hA5 frame, still receives 8'hA5 on this RTL.\n(2) testbench_bug. The repro's expected values come from the 8N1 contract and the transmitted byte, not from RTL output. Refuted for this repro if its byte check fails while its start-bit, stop-bit and idle checks pass. That points at payload corruption, not sampling misalignment, which would also break the start and stop checks.\n(3) infrastructure. Unlikely: [run:run-0002] built and reached $finish with a deterministic 1-of-4 check failure. Refuted further if the platform's independent run of this new testbench fails the same single check.\n(4) spec_ambiguity. Rejected because the RTL's header clause explicitly fixes the behaviour: start while busy is ignored.\n\nCONCLUSION: rtl_bug. Confirming it depends on the platform's simulator.run (expect=fail) of the attached testbench."}], "files": [{"path": "uart_tx_rootcause_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking repro: start pulse during a frame must not alter the transmitted byte", "summary": "Repro for [requirement:req-d10c4df532] against [artifact:prj-d4a591eb4b.design-under-investigation.a1].\n\nStimulus: sends 8'hA5 with CLKS_PER_BIT=4. During data bit 1 it pulses start with 8'h3C.\n\nSampling: the serial line is sampled once per bit-time, starting about 1.5 clocks after start is accepted.\n\nFour checks, with expected values from the 8N1 contract:\n- start bit is 0\n- received byte is 8'hA5\n- stop bit is 1\n- line is idle high and not busy after the frame\n\nExpected result: fails the byte check on the RTL under investigation and passes on RTL that ignores start while busy. It prints exactly one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict with the run nonce before $finish. A watchdog counts a hang as a failure.", "entry": "uart_tx_rootcause_tb"}], "tool_runs": ["run-0001", "run-0002"], "claims": ["Expected: on the RTL under investigation, the attached testbench receives 8'hBD instead of 8'hA5 (bits 3 and 6 come from 8'h3C) and reports 3 passed, 1 failed. This has not been run by me.", "Expected: on RTL without the pre-case hold assignment, the attached testbench reports 4 passed, 0 failed. This has not been run by me."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Independent review is still required (review_record). The platform must run simulator.run with expect=fail on uart_tx_rootcause_tb.v before review. The upstream triage testbench uart_tx_triage_repro.v was not inspected; only its run summary was available."}
